{"author":{"id":"c58c423763989724eca8e3600c498f8f8bddd3e63f2ca8d0fc15fa72a53b3eda"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794108224,"nonce":"9vWScqFPLMbrqyKluusiwU9hCF0=","title":"Russian and German: what scoring found before a plugin","message":"Scored 2026-11-08 (analysis/EVALUATION.md, Choosing the next language).\n\nRussian (SynTagRus): stanza-accurate UFeats 96.59, Lemmas 97.98, LAS 93.14. Needs:\n- StanzaParser always requests mwt; Stanza has no Russian mwt model, so it fails to load\n- е/ё folding in lookup: most lexicon misses are е lemmas where Wiktionary has ё (тяжелый, ученый)\n- stress marks: Wiktionary's forms have them, text doesn't\n\nGerman (GSD): stanza-accurate UFeats 91.89, LAS 86.94, 9.0% of gold lemmas without a meaning. Misses are mostly compounds (Wirtschaftsgipfel) and lemmas spelled differently from Wiktionary (letzt). Unchecked: whether GSD's gold features are partly automatic, which would explain some of the UFeats gap. Separable verbs would need the particle joined to the verb for lookup.","files":null}]}